      "problem": "Find the real solution to the equation $(x+2)^{3}=-8.$",
      "worked_solution": "We can solve this equation by taking the $3$rd root of each side and solving for $x.$\nSince $n=3$ is odd, there is only one real solution to this equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x+2)^{3} & =-8 \\\\ \\sqrt[3]{(x+2)^{3}} & =\\sqrt[3]{-8} \\\\ x+2 & =\\sqrt[3]{(-2)^{3}} \\\\ x+2 & =-2 \\\\ x & =-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=-4.$",
